From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 07:18:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Vulkan: robustBufferAccess when the device has it
 (PS3RECOMP_VK_ROBUST=0 off)

Symptom (#129 and a second report, AMD RX 6600 and RX 5700 XT on
Windows, v0.6.0): the game closes a few seconds into level 1 with no
error line, after rendering stalls for 1 to 2 s; the same build works on
NVIDIA. That fits a GPU hang ended by Windows' 2 s TDR. Not yet
confirmed on those cards.

Candidate fix: the device was made without robustBufferAccess, so a
shader or vertex fetch reading past the end of a buffer (a guest index
beyond its vertex data, a program reading constants past what was
bound) is undefined behaviour, which NVIDIA's driver tolerates and
AMD's may answer with a hang. With the feature such a read gives zeros
or a value from inside the buffer. Every Vulkan device reports it; it is
enabled whenever reported, and PS3RECOMP_VK_ROBUST=0 turns it off for
A/B runs. The log says which: "robustBufferAccess: on", "off
(PS3RECOMP_VK_ROBUST=0)" or "off (the device does not have it)".

robustBufferAccess2 and robustImageAccess are not asked for: they need
VK_EXT_robustness2 (or image robustness) and a feature chain on top of
the ones Reflex, FSR 3 and DLSS already build, they cost more on AMD,
and the guest's programs sample their images, which is already clamped
or wrapped. Written from the Vulkan specification.
---
 libs/video/rsx_vulkan_backend.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_vulkan_backend.c b/libs/video/rsx_vulkan_backend.c
index b0fbf61..13a01d6 100644
--- a/libs/video/rsx_vulkan_backend.c
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_vulkan_backend.c
@@ -7395,6 +7395,21 @@ static int vk_init_all(u32 width, u32 height, const char* title)
      * a run with an upscaler are built ahead by one without (2061) */
     want.independentBlend = have.independentBlend;
     s_vk.indep_blend_ok = have.independentBlend ? 1 : 0;
+    /* robustBufferAccess (2083): a shader or vertex fetch that reads past the end of a buffer gets zeros or a value
+     * from inside the buffer instead of whatever memory is there. Undefined behaviour without it: NVIDIA's driver
+     * has been seen to tolerate it where AMD's can hang the GPU, and a hang becomes a lost device after Windows' 2 s
+     * TDR, the candidate cause of #129 (AMD RX 5000/6000 closing a few seconds into level 1). Every Vulkan device
+     * has the feature; PS3RECOMP_VK_ROBUST=0 turns it off, for A/B runs (default on). robustBufferAccess2 and
+     * robustImageAccess (VK_EXT_robustness2, image robustness) are not asked for: they need an extension and a
+     * feature chain on top of the Reflex/FSR 3/DLSS ones and cost more on AMD, and the guest's programs sample
+     * images, which are already clamped or wrapped. */
+    { const char* e = getenv("PS3RECOMP_VK_ROBUST");
+      const int f = rsx_vk_env_flag(e);
+      if (f < 0) VK_LOG("PS3RECOMP_VK_ROBUST=%s not understood (0 or 1), on\n", e);
+      const int asked = !e || f != 0;
+      want.robustBufferAccess = asked ? have.robustBufferAccess : VK_FALSE;
+      VK_LOG("robustBufferAccess: %s\n", want.robustBufferAccess ? "on"
+                                         : !asked ? "off (PS3RECOMP_VK_ROBUST=0)" : "off (the device does not have it)"); }
     if (!s_vk.indep_blend_ok && s_tm.want)
         VK_LOG("temporal: no independentBlend on this device, camera motion only\n");
     { VkPhysicalDeviceProperties dp; pvkGetPhysicalDeviceProperties(s_vk.phys, &dp);
